Implanner plans, ranks, and automates colonist implants. Decide who should get which bionics, and the mod queues the crafting and schedules the surgeries to make it happen.

Instead of micromanaging medical operations and crafting bills one at a time, you design implant plans - reusable lists of desired implants - and hand them to colonists. Implanner tracks per-colonist progress, shows what is blocking the next step, and (if you let it) runs the whole production-to-surgery pipeline for you.

[h1]Key Features[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Implant Plans:[/b] A plan is a reusable set of implant goals. Assign the same plan to any number of colonists, and edit it in a conflict-aware editor with an anatomy filter.
[*][b]Plan Inheritance:[/b] A plan can extend another plan: a Soldier plan builds on your colony baseline, overriding only where it wants something better.
[*][b]Conflict Aware:[/b] Which implants can coexist is derived from actual game data (mods included), mirroring the game's own surgery rules. Selecting a conflicting implant simply overrides the other - the click is the choice, and the editor tells you what gets replaced.
[*][b]Star Rankings:[/b] Drag implants into star tiers to decide what matters most; within a tier you arrange the exact order. Rankings are yours alone - everything starts at three stars and the mod never rearranges them.
[*][b]Overview Table:[/b] A colony-wide table of colonists with plan, progress, next operation and blockers, plus grouping, sorting and a per-colonist detail panel.
[*][b]Automated Production:[/b] Implanner counts the implants your plans still need and queues crafting bills at your benches - as ordinary bills you can see and touch. Bills for no-longer-needed implants are cleaned up automatically.
[*][b]Automated Surgery:[/b] Operations are scheduled when the implant is in stock and a capable doctor is available. Implant items are reserved so haulers and traders do not run off with them.
[*][b]Doctor Skill Floor:[/b] By default the required surgeon skill tracks your best available doctor in each colony; turn auto off to set a manual minimum.
[*][b]Implant Reserves:[/b] Hold a configurable number of each implant back from automation, so there is always stock for manual operations.
[*][b]Multi-Colony:[/b] Plans are global; production, reservations and surgery run per colony, and colonists are matched to the colony they are actually at.
[*][b]Modded Implants:[/b] Implants from other mods appear automatically, no compatibility patches needed. Works with any DLC mix - only content you actually have is offered.
[*][b]Designed for Performance:[/b] Extensive caching, rendering from pre-calculated caches, scoped invalidation, no per-tick logic.
[*][b]Multiplayer:[/b] Fully [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2606448745]RimWorld Multiplayer[/url] compatible - all automation is deterministic, so every client computes the same result.
[/list]

[h1]How Automation Works[/h1]
[list]
[*]Production works down your star tiers: by default Implanner finishes the current tier before starting the next, so top-ranked implants get built and installed first.
[*]A crafting bill is only created when every ingredient keeps its configured reserve after the full cost of the bill. Baseline reserves ship for steel, plasteel, gold, components and advanced components; every reserve is overridable, including down to zero.
[*]You control how many benches per colony Implanner may occupy, a minimum crafting skill for its bills, and whether it may only use idle benches.
[*]With intermediates enabled, missing ingredients that are themselves craftable (components, drugs, and similar) are queued too.
[*]When an implant is in stock, it is reserved for a specific colonist and the operation is added to their surgery list; your doctors take it from there.
[*]An installed implant that already excludes the planned one counts as done: an archotech leg satisfies a bionic-leg goal instead of scheduling a pointless downgrade.
[/list]

[h1]Worth Knowing[/h1]
[list]
[*]Implanner is about implants only: weapons, apparel and utility gear are deliberately out of scope (the overview can display them, but nothing acts on them).
[*]Only ordinary humanlike colonists are plannable; mutant-only implants such as the ghoul kit are excluded.
[*]Automation options live in their own tab: iteration strategy, bench limits, skill requirements, resource reserves and implant reserves.
[*]Everything the automation does is visible in the game as ordinary bills and surgery entries - there is no hidden machinery.
[/list]

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]
[list]
[*]Safe to add to existing saves: installed implants are recognized and count toward plan progress.
[*]Multi-floor mods (MultiFloors, Strata, As above so below II): planning, rankings and progress tracking work fully; automation stands down, because medical bills cannot fetch ingredients across floors in those mods. Scheduling operations that can never complete would be worse.
[*]Requires [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2009463077]Harmony[/url].
[/list]

Found a bug or an incompatible mod? Let me know in the comments.

